WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Models and assumptions. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Name what a diagram leaves out

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: A model is a useful selective representation. Record assumptions and limits so readers know when results may fail.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: A fixed Cd drag equation omits changing yaw and flow separation; keep its conditions beside the answer.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Model-limit audit

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: A system diagram is a model, not a finished vehicle or proof of roadworthiness.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Name what a diagram leaves out
